summary:
  The settle swap stops taking a job number of its own and goes out under
  whatever the last rebuild or swap carried.

history:
  The swap shares the rebuild's lock and its thirty seconds, and unlike a
  rebuild it leaves the module map standing, so a second swap can go out
  the moment the first one's time is up. With one number between them the
  first swap's late answer is the second one's: the lock opens while the
  second shell is still fading a speaker over, and the first one's module
  is adopted next to it. The rebuild's launch line is a separate string and
  bumping only that one leaves this road open.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
          app.exec(": PW_LBSWAP " + ReloopLogic.stamp(_combineLoadSeq, ++_reloopJob) + "; " + cmds + "true"

replace:
          app.exec(": PW_LBSWAP " + ReloopLogic.stamp(_combineLoadSeq, _reloopJob) + "; " + cmds + "true"

expect:
  Killed by tst_syncengine::test_a_hung_swap_cannot_answer_for_the_swap_that_followed_it.
  Line-neutral.
